Subject: [PATCH 031] pci: gate the 2.5GT/s link speed lift by Vendor:Device

The ZTE ZX279128S root ports come up trained at Gen1 x1: U-Boot/cspboot leaves
Target Link Speed at 2.5GT/s, and the vendor product only ever runs that link at
Gen1 -- its own MT7916 main function reports LnkSta=0x1011 (speed 1) for the
whole life of the product (device/backup/vendor-ep0-config.txt).

This tree's pcie_failed_link_retrain() has no Vendor:Device restriction, so as
soon as the root port is enumerated it sees LnkCtl2.TLS==2.5GT/s with a higher
LnkCap.SLS and lifts the restriction:

    pci 0000:00:00.0: removing 2.5GT/s downstream link speed restriction

and the link retrains to Gen2 -- one generation faster than the vendor stack has
ever run it, on a x1 link. Both failures we have on this board sit in DMA bursts
(the MT7916 firmware download, and client association).

Upstream later tightened this same helper to a Vendor:Device allow-list, because
lifting a speed restriction that firmware deliberately installed is not safe in
general. Backport that gate: ASMedia ASM2824 keeps its behaviour, the ZTE port
stays at the speed its bootloader trained. No config-space poke and no retrain
request is involved, which is what makes this different (and safe) compared to
writing LnkCtl2.TLS at runtime.

--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c	2026-10-14 15:53:40.619462904 +0800
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c	2026-10-14 15:53:40.764947963 +0800
@@ -93,6 +93,10 @@
  */
 int pcie_failed_link_retrain(struct pci_dev *dev)
 {
+	static const struct pci_device_id ids[] = {
+		{ PCI_VDEVICE(ASMEDIA, 0x2824) }, /* ASMedia ASM2824 */
+		{}
+	};
 	u16 lnksta, lnkctl2, oldlnkctl2;
 	int ret = -ENOTTY;
 	u32 lnkcap;
@@ -113,7 +117,8 @@
 	pcie_capability_read_word(dev, PCI_EXP_LNKCTL2, &lnkctl2);
 	pcie_capability_read_dword(dev, PCI_EXP_LNKCAP, &lnkcap);
 	if ((lnkctl2 & PCI_EXP_LNKCTL2_TLS) == PCI_EXP_LNKCTL2_TLS_2_5GT &&
-	    (lnkcap & PCI_EXP_LNKCAP_SLS) != PCI_EXP_LNKCAP_SLS_2_5GB) {
+	    (lnkcap & PCI_EXP_LNKCAP_SLS) != PCI_EXP_LNKCAP_SLS_2_5GB &&
+	    pci_match_id(ids, dev)) {
 		pci_info(dev, "removing 2.5GT/s downstream link speed restriction\n");
 		ret = pcie_set_target_speed(dev, PCIE_LNKCAP_SLS2SPEED(lnkcap), false);
 		if (ret)
